#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:5
#: 4dd1e865a14a425e857b324e62abbfaf
msgid "Dock Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:7
#: 9e3951bef19e426593de73cb18dac4f6
msgid "The DOCK mode maneuvers a vehicle towards a stationary docking target automatically. Currently, we support docking with the help of a camera attached to a companion computer. The companion computer estimates the pose of the marker (`ArucoMarker/AprilTag <https://april.eecs.umich.edu/software/apriltag>`__) placed at the docking station and sends `LANDING_TARGET <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#LANDING_TARGET>`__ mavlink messages to the vehicle which are then processed by the precision landing library (`AC_PrecLand <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AC_PrecLand>`__) to estimate the position of the docking target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:13
#: 58b6cc49c377436f9138945ed25eaebf
msgid "Successful tests have been conducted using the OpenMV camera as a companion computer to perform auto-docking. However, any companion computer equipped with an RGB camera (like OpenMV camera, Raspberry Pi, Jetson Nano etc.) which can estimate pose of marker placed at docking target and generate the  `LANDING_TARGET <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#LANDING_TARGET>`__ mavlink messages to the vehicle's autopilot can be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:18
#: aba979578f75474d8b8983392f5189bd
msgid "The OpenMV Camera"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:20
#: 180c5064885b4f1b9112c2d0df28bf5e
msgid "OpenMV camera is a pocket sized camera board which is capable of performing various computer vision tasks. It can transmit the required mavlink messages over its UART interface and hence it can be used as a companion computer to perform auto-docking. The camera can be purchased directly from `openmv.io <https://openmv.io/collections/cams>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:25
#: bc1d805ac5fd47d8a0e0e5504f23e4d6
msgid "Connection to Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:27
#: eb64bb600aeb40c592e9ac61eab8bea6
msgid "The companion computer needs to be connected a serial port on the autopilot via its UART interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:33
#: 5baee56ff420429a9bc5a0976ee7ca52
msgid "Connect the camera’s P4, VIN and GND pins to one of the autopilot’s serial ports as shown above. In the image above the OpenMV cam is connected to a Pixhawk’s Telem2 port. The connection scheme would be similar for the other companion computers too. The user just needs to make a connection between TX pin on the companion computer to RX pin of the telemetry port on the autopilot and power up the companion computer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:36
#: f2dcccae061a4e0e99e65f50253cb112
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL <SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 1 (MAVLink) if using Serial2/Telem2, if connected to another serial port use the corresponding SERIALx_PROTOCOL parameter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:37
#: 2804bf635c2f4fc38c4c3d36726b19d3
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL2_BAUD <SERIAL2_BAUD>` = 115"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:40
#: c47e4a6a8d8c4b55bf200f726e700e7c
msgid "Generating AprilTag Markers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:46
#: ff5bd03a77b74442bc643ddc7d03d497
msgid "The OpenMV camera has capability to detect the AprilTags. The OpenMV IDE comes with built-in AprilTag generator. The steps to generate an AprilTag using the same are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:48
#: edd2bed4e32a432d9f1140a49f391eb5
msgid "Go to Tools -> Machine Vision -> AprilTag generator -> TAG36H11 Family (587 Tags - Recommended). This will open a small dialog box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:49
#: 667eec12cbc842bab507b0956241ad9c
msgid "Set the range of tags you want to generate. For eg. if you want to generate tag number 1, set Min and Max to 1. You can also generate a range of tags at once by setting the Min and Max values accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:50
#: 052b4add2f834e70870d0140bd6fa894
msgid "Click ok and save the tags to the desired directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:52
#: a79a218787d649b5a4a1ea044e817b25
msgid "After successfully generating the tag, the user can print it out and place it vertically at the docking target. The default printing size of tag as per the `example script <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/blob/master/scripts/examples/07-Interface-Library/02-MAVLink/mavlink_apriltags_landing_target.py>`__ in following section is 165 mm. A tag of this size is obtained by simply printing the generated tag image on an A4 size sheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:58
#: 0469f94c398c45c1b78a69b2c8e88ab0
msgid "The maximum range of marker detection while using the `example script <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/blob/master/scripts/examples/07-Interface-Library/02-MAVLink/mavlink_apriltags_landing_target.py>`__ mentioned in next section and a 165 mm marker is around 1.5 - 2 m. This range can be increased by using a marker of bigger size. The maximum range of around 4 m has been successfully obtained by using a 380 mm marker during the tests. Instructions about modifying the script for using bigger markers are discussed in next section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:63
#: 2968a6eb89d642fb8e5b22ad3869ac3f
msgid "Uploading Code to the Camera"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:65
#: f5d6de77a06b4425bb427441c8159aed
msgid "The OpenMV camera can be programmed using the OpenMV IDE. Detailed instructions to do so can be found `here <http://docs.openmv.io/openmvcam/tutorial/index.html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:67
#: a83deed14622401f818a55a53d18dcf3
msgid "Connect the OpenMV camera to your PC using  a micro USB cable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:68
#: 9de41f22db374c749a56b2a83c2946ab
msgid "Open the OpenMV IDE and click the connect button at the bottom left corner of the IDE window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:69
#: 862302ff29974cb8acc49170cc4f4198
msgid "Go to file menu, create new file and copy `this <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/blob/master/scripts/examples/07-Interface-Library/02-MAVLink/mavlink_apriltags_landing_target.py>`__ script to the editor window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:71
#: a61e0c88419b4afcb71c6026d9255ee9
msgid "Set the tag number and the size of the marker `here <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/blob/8587f8d7c6d2c23b75e86154c73ae45bc8935bc0/scripts/examples/07-Interface-Library/02-MAVLink/mavlink_apriltags_landing_target.py#L29>`__. The size must be measured from edge to edge (including the black border) in mm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:73
#: 5621ad65f539442580737fee5e3c410e
msgid "To upload the code to the camera go to Tools menu and click on `Save open script to OpenMV Cam (as main.py)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:74
#: 4c58ca9888bb484680b5235e51a1a25c
msgid "Done! Now you can remove the micro USB cable and power up the camera using an external power source. If the script is successfully running, you should see a RED or GREEN LED blinking on the camera. The led flashes GREEN when the marker is in sight of the camera whereas it flashes RED when the camera can't see the marker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:78
#: 7da772b7401848a5a819f9ef6eb4634c
msgid "Mounting to the vehicle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:80
#: 903bcefb63304b05859cacb3ba0f2458
msgid "The camera should be mounted at the front of the vehicle. The camera board should be mounted such that the camera edge with the lens is upwards (i.e., away from the ground). This is the default setup configuration that we think would be used in most of the cases. However, support for mounting the camera at the back and in different mounting orientations is also provided. If you want to mount the camera in any other configuration, please don't forget to set the related `PLND_XXX` parameters accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:86
#: 4cd7674d380b479a82f6e5051675d5cb
msgid "The precision landing library also relies on the vehicle's compass to construct the target vector. Any kind of `magnetic interference <https://ardupilot.org/rover/docs/common-magnetic-interference.html>`__ in the vehicle's compass may lead to the vehicle behaving inappropriately during the docking process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:90
#: 46d9d84bf4444d769e9ca051643dad8c
msgid "Setup through GCS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:92
#: 6565999fc7c2453bbec5b19e04456c37
msgid "The following parameters are needed to be set to enable the precision landing using a companion computer on the rover."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:94
#: 42d4403d4269467aaacbaba8efe4263c
msgid ":ref:`PLND_ENABLED <PLND_ENABLED>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:95
#: 5bf5f65ccb2a425eacbc82dd91fbed8c
msgid ":ref:`PLND_TYPE <PLND_TYPE>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:97
#: 0e18bd65fb124a219da500532df33def
msgid "You would need to reboot the vehicle once you set up the above mentioned parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:99
#: 1f6f267f5e534b4b90cfee8033e23d33
msgid "If you are mounting the camera in any configuration other than the default configuration mentioned in the previous section, please set the following parameters appropriately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:101
#: a7a01fb2fcc44923b19445fc0ebe8920
msgid ":ref:`PLND_CAM_POS_X <PLND_CAM_POS_X>`, :ref:`PLND_CAM_POS_Y <PLND_CAM_POS_Y>`, :ref:`PLND_CAM_POS_Z <PLND_CAM_POS_Z>`: Position of camera in body frame (in m)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:102
#: 84267fc7a2ef4caab041f212671de672
msgid ":ref:`PLND_ORIENT <PLND_ORIENT>`: Orientation of camera on vehicles body. The camera can be mounted at the front or at the back of the vehicle's body"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:103
#: fe71a486d29643369062cbbad3bc71c6
msgid ":ref:`PLND_YAW_ALIGN <PLND_YAW_ALIGN>`: Angle of rotation of camera from default configuration to mounted configuration around the axis pointing out from it's lens (in centi degrees)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:105
#: b9168911a3ca48e08b637fe20c1118c8
msgid "The docking process can be fine tuned using the following parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:107
#: 72980133db1349108e4f91622aee1717
msgid ":ref:`DOCK_SPEED <DOCK_SPEED>`: The maximum speed limit at the which the vehicle can maneuver in the dock mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:108
#: 87a053b7263b4c2e8b2a7b11d6247088
msgid ":ref:`DOCK_HDG_CORR_EN <DOCK_HDG_CORR_EN>`: To enable the heading correction while docking. This would enable the vehicle to dock head-on onto the docking station even if the dock mode is switched while the vehicle is not exactly in front of the dock. Note that this feature works only if :ref:`DOCK_DIR <DOCK_DIR>` parameter is correctly set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:109
#: 2bb6a5cd614343409e1f6056ee915ee2
msgid ":ref:`DOCK_DIR <DOCK_DIR>`: This is the compass direction in which the vehicle is desired to head while docking. This direction is opposite to the direction in which the docking station is facing. For eg., if the docking station is facing North, the vehicle is desired to dock from the south and hence the parameter should be set with the value 180 degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:110
#: c32246d01d434cb8838d29c77c308e3c
msgid ":ref:`DOCK_HDG_CORR_WT <DOCK_HDG_CORR_WT>`: This parameter defines how aggressively the vehicle tries to corrects its heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:111
#: b0957200164e44cf8c01d26d29a67b0d
msgid ":ref:`DOCK_STOP_DIST <DOCK_STOP_DIST>`: The distance from the docking station at which the vehicle should stop (in meter)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dock-mode.rst:115
#: e7f80073ad0149dc8c72fd9035bb942c
msgid "Be prepared to retake control if there are sudden unexpected movements (Change mode to Hold or manual)."
msgstr ""
